WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.168
-Everyone's probably asking you

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.402
the same questions
about "Game of Thrones"

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:05.739
and it's the final season.
but I was gonna ask you,

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:08.608
do you have a top five maybe

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:10.409
iconic moments
of your character,

00:00:10.409 --> 00:00:12.312
of Arya's moments on the show?

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:14.413
-I do.
I mean, there are so many.

00:00:14.413 --> 00:00:18.250
But in terms of things
that have really defined her,

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:22.522
I think number one would be
Ned's beheading in season 1.

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:24.491
That was what
spiraled her whole arc.

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:25.624
-Yes.

00:00:25.624 --> 00:00:30.496
-And then she was with the Hound
for a long time.

00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:32.732
I think there was a line in
maybe season three

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.600
where she was like, "One day,
I'm gonna stick a knife

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.669
through your eye
and out the back of your skull."

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.538
That was, like,
a pretty defining moment

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:40.940
when you realized how --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.876
how messed up in the head
that she'd become.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.077
-Yeah.
-And in season five,

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:47.447
I think she threw away
her original costume.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:50.182
And I was in that costume for
like four years or something.

00:00:50.182 --> 00:00:52.052
So, she threw that
into the water,

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:54.954
and it was
a really emotional moment.

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:59.259
I guess last season,
she reunited with Sansa again,

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:01.528
so that was a pretty big moment.

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:03.996
And then they both united
and killed Littlefinger,

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:06.699
and that's pretty --
-That's like kind of -- yeah.

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:09.035
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's not bad.

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:12.505
This is the final --
the final season.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:14.807
Everyone's been waiting.

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:16.942
Can you tell me anything?

00:01:16.942 --> 00:01:19.278
Are you allowed
to talk about anything?

00:01:19.278 --> 00:01:22.348
-I've decided to just keep
a tight lip on everything.

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:27.086
HBO have sent out a lot of memos
recently about just say nothing.

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:28.921
-Yeah.
-So there's really nothing

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:31.091
that I can say.
They would absolutely kill me.

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:32.658
-You couldn't give --
You couldn't give

00:01:32.658 --> 00:01:35.795
one little spoiler,
one little hint of a

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:38.097
a little --
a crumb is all I ask.

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:39.432
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.267
Milady. Just a crumb
is all I'm asking for.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.069
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:44.971
-Um...I don't know.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:49.609
Like, during shooting,
the final days

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.544
were really, like, emotional,

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:53.046
saying goodbye
to all of the cast.

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:56.582
Because when I found out that
Arya died in the second episode,

00:01:56.582 --> 00:02:00.854
I was --
[ Audience gasps, laughs ]

00:02:00.854 --> 00:02:03.723
-What?

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.925
Are you kidding me?

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:07.760
That's a spoiler.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.128
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:11.397
-Is this live?
-No.

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.800
-We can edit that out.
-Are you serious?

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.400
-Yeah.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:16.536
-Dude, yeah, totally.

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:18.504
-They're still
gonna tweet about it.

00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:21.007
-No. Don't worry about it.
Are you serious?

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:22.341
It's fine.
-I'm really sorry.

00:02:22.341 --> 00:02:23.308
-No, don't worry about it.
No, it's fine.

00:02:23.308 --> 00:02:25.812
-Okay.
-We can edit it, right?

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:28.280
Yeah.
We can edit it out.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.415
Don't worry about it.
-Okay.

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:30.849
-Yeah.
Don't worry about it.

00:02:30.849 --> 00:02:33.585
No one's gonna --
It's fine.

00:02:33.585 --> 00:02:35.788
It's cool.
Let's just start --

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:36.990
Can we do applause,
and I'll just go

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.591
from the applause
and go into it again?

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:41.794
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:45.698
Let's talk about, uh...

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:46.866
Let's talk about the final --

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.100
Let's talk about
the final season.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:53.973
-I'm...

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:56.275
-Um...

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:58.311
Is she okay?

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:03.182
Is she okay?

00:03:03.182 --> 00:03:07.253
We'll just go...

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.488
-April Fools!

00:03:09.488 --> 00:03:10.590
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.191
♪♪

00:03:12.191 --> 00:03:15.061
-You were so good!
Oh, my gosh!

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:17.430
We got you guys so bad!

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.732
Maisie Williams, everybody!

